pipeline-out/

# The published run is committed on purpose.
#
# It is what the dashboard reads, and the whole point of a project's dashboard
# URL is that it can be handed to somebody else. Ignored, the link worked only
# on the machine that produced it: a fresh clone answered "no manifest" and
# View PDF 404ed. Each run is about 18MB of PNGs and filled PDFs and replaces
# the last one wholesale, so the history carries a copy per published run -
# that is the cost of the link being real, and `git rm -r --cached "Current
# Form Output"` takes it back.
#
# pipeline-out/ above stays ignored: it is scratch, and everything worth
# keeping out of it is copied into the published run.
Current Form Output/index.json.tmp

# A guest's saved projects (dev-server.js /api/guest-library). Personal
# work, one machine's library - never committed.
guest-library/
